 ```
 
+### Generated API Types
+
+`frontend/src/lib/api-generated.ts` is generated from the backend's own pydantic
+models. **Never edit it by hand.** Refresh it after changing an API route or a
+response model:
+
+```bash
+cd frontend
+pnpm gen:api:export     # 1. export the internal spec (needs the Python env)
+pnpm gen:api            # 2. regenerate the types (needs node_modules)
+```
+
+Commit the regenerated file together with the backend change that prompted it.
+
+The two specs are different artifacts. `docs/openapi.json` is the **public** API
+document: `web/app.py` hides every route and re-enables a 16-entry `_PUBLIC_API`
+allowlist, so it carries 12 paths. Type generation needs the whole surface
+(~350 paths), which is what `--internal` writes to `frontend/openapi.json` — a
+gitignored build artifact. The public spec is untouched by this flow.
+
+Types in `frontend/src/lib/api.ts` are migrated onto the generated schemas
+incrementally:
+
+```ts
+export type DashboardStats = components["schemas"]["DashboardStatsResponse"]
+```
+
+An alias cannot drift: rename the field on the backend and `tsc` fails at every
+call site that read the old name. The interfaces still hand-written there are
+the ones whose endpoint declares no `response_model`, so the spec has nothing to
+generate from — add the response model and the type becomes migratable.
+`src/lib/__tests__/api-generated.test.ts` pins the aliases and fails if the file
+was regenerated from the public spec by mistake.
+
 ### Environment
 
 ```bash
@@ -357,6 +391,7 @@ Before submitting, ensure:
 - [ ] `uv run ruff check src/ tests/` passes
 - [ ] `uv run pytest` passes
 - [ ] `cd frontend && pnpm build` passes (if frontend changes)
+- [ ] `pnpm gen:api` output committed, if any API route or response model changed
 - [ ] i18n strings added to `messages/en/` only — other locales auto-translate on commit (if UI text changed)
 - [ ] New features have corresponding tests
 - [ ] PR description explains **what** and **why**
